meta {
  name: Create Text Attribute
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_text",
    "type": "TextAttribute"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.type: eq TextAttribute
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1`, for Products (Phase 2b) to
  reference in its `attributes` map.

  `201 Created`. `label` defaults to the same value as `name` when
  omitted (must match the `^[a-z0-9_]+$` pattern the spec declares for
  `label`, so `name` values that are already lowercase/underscore-safe
  work as a default label for free).

  Also confirmed: `group_ids: ["6a9f1b872b6fd055ffb7c7df"]` (referencing
  `05-Product-Attribute-Groups`'s fixture) is **accepted without error**
  on create, but is **not** reflected back in either the create response
  or a subsequent `GET`/`_fields=group_ids` -- inconclusive whether the
  group linkage actually persists. Flag as an open item; worth re-checking
  from the attribute-group side (`GET
  /product-attribute-groups/{id}/{path}` for a members-list-shaped
  subpath) in a later session.

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  Same `409 Conflict {"errors":[{"name":"AlreadyExists","description":"An
  attribute with the same name already exists"}]}` behavior as
  `05-Product-Attribute-Groups/Create Product Attribute Group.bru` once
  the fixture already exists.
}
